<article class="enc-article">
<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Amir ibn Abd al-Wahhab</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1489–<a href="/years/1517">1517</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Amir II</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Amir ibn Abd al-Wahhab was the last major sultan of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tahirid-dynasty">Tahirid dynasty</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a>, reigning from 1489 to 1517. A patron of learning and builder, he founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amiriya-madrasa">Amiriya Madrasa</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/radaa">Rada'a</a>. His realm faced the Portuguese in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-sea">Red Sea</a> and in 1515 a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluk</a> expedition from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, which defeated his forces. He was killed in 1517 near Sanaa, and Tahirid rule collapsed.</p></div>
